%I A397206 #24 Aug 13 2026 00:58:23
%S A397206 1,1,3,7,23,83,353,1575,7089,34205,174649,956637,5561653,34731283
%N A397206 Number of words of length n over an infinite alphabet such that all prefixes satisfy c(i) >= c(j) if f(i) < f(j) where c(i) is the number of occurrences of the letter i and f(i) = floor(sqrt(2*i) + 1/2).
%C A397206 The relations of the letters form a partial order of the natural numbers shown below:
%C A397206   ...
%C A397206  4 5 6
%C A397206   2 3
%C A397206    1
%C A397206 All terms are odd.
%H A397206 John Tyler Rascoe, <a href="/A397206/a397206.py.txt">Python code</a>.
%e A397206 All prefixes of the word (1,3,2,1,4,6) satisfy the required conditions so this is counted under a(6) = 353.
%e A397206 a(1) = 1: (1).
%e A397206 a(2) = 3: (1,1), (1,2), (1,3).
%e A397206 a(3) = 7: (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,1), (1,1,3), (1,3,1), (1,2,3), (1,3,2).
